00.0,1200.0,Matched,Exact match\nComcast Business,Nov 2025,189.0,189.0,Matched,Exact match\nGoogle Cloud Platform,Nov 2025,410.0,410.0,Matched,Exact match\nAWS,Nov 2025,1100.5,1100.5,Matched,Exact match\nSalesforce,Nov 2025,500.0,500.0,Matched,Exact match\nSlack,Nov 2025,175.0,175.0,Matched,Exact match\nMicrosoft 365,Nov 2025,99.99,99.99,Matched,Exact match\nBlue Shield of California,Dec 2025,1200.0,1200.0,Matched,Exact match\nComcast Business,Dec 2025,189.0,189.0,Matched,Exact match\nGoogle Cloud Platform,Dec 2025,340.0,340.0,Matched,Exact match\nAWS,Dec 2025,975.0,975.0,Matched,Exact match\nSalesforce,Dec 2025,500.0,500.0,Matched,Exact match\nSlack,Dec 2025,150.0,150.0,Matched,Exact match\nMicrosoft 365,Dec 2025,99.99,0.0,Unmatched,No matching QBO entry\n', 'type': 'function_call_output'}, {'id': 'msg_00e30ce9a51f3b1e0069a26692977c81958254cb98c14c55ea', 'content': [{'annotations': [], 'text': 'Here’s the reconciliation summary for all 84 invoices against the 2025 QBO vendor summary, and the discrepancies I found.\n\n### 1) What I reconciled\n\nVendors (7):\n- Blue Shield of California  \n- Comcast Business  \n- Google Cloud Platform  \n- AWS  \n- Salesforce  \n- Slack  \n- Microsoft 365  \n\nPeriods:\n- Jan 2025 through Dec 2025 (12 months)\n\nFor each invoice, I matched:\n- Vendor name (direct name match to QBO row)  \n- Period: invoice service period in month/year → `Mon YYYY`  \n- Invoice amount vs. QBO monthly total for that vendor\n\nAll 84 invoice/vendor/month combinations were sent to the reconciliation tool and classified.\n\n---\n\n### 2) Overall reconciliation results (per tool output)\n\n- Total invoice lines: **84**\n- Status counts:\n  - **Matched (exact): 80**\n  - **Partial: 2**\n  - **Unmatched: 2**\n- Totals:\n  - **Total invoiced:** \\$42,769.83  \n  - **Total in QBO:** \\$42,457.34  \n  - **Overall difference:** **\\$312.49 short in QBO vs. invoices**\n\n---\n\n### 3) Discrepancies (partials and unmatched)\n\nThese are the items needing attention.\n\n#### A. Partial matches (amount differs, vendor & month align)\n\n1) **Google Cloud Platform – Feb 2025**\n- Invoice: **\\$425.00**\n- QBO: **\\$412.50**  \n- Difference: **\\$12.50 short in QBO**  \n- Likely causes: credit applied, partial posting, or rounding/mis-keyed amount.\n\n2) **AWS – Apr 2025**\n- Invoice: **\\$1,050.00**\n- QBO: **\\$1,000.00**  \n- Difference: **\\$50.00 short in QBO**  \n- Likely causes: under-accrual, discount/credit, or a portion booked elsewhere.\n\nSubtotal of partial differences:\n- **\\$12.50 + \\$50.00 = \\$62.50** short in QBO\n\n---\n\n#### B. Unmatched items (invoice exists, no QBO expense for that period/vendor)\n\n1) **Slack – Jan 2025**\n- Invoice: **\\$150.00**\n- QBO: **\\$0.00** (no Jan Slack spend shown)  \n- Issue: January Slack bill not reflected in QBO for that month.  \n- Possibilities:  \n  - Posted in a different month  \n  - Misclassified under another vendor/account  \n  - Not recorded.\n\n2) **Microsoft 365 – Dec 2025**\n- Invoice: **\\$99.99**\n- QBO: **\\$0.00** (no Dec Microsoft 365 spend shown)  \n- Issue: December Microsoft 365 invoice missing from QBO.  \n- Possibilities:  \n  - Expense not yet recorded (timing)  \n  - Posted to a different vendor name or account  \n  - Paid but not coded to an expense (e.g., to Prepaid, Suspense).\n\nSubtotal of unmatched differences:\n- **\\$150.00 + \\$99.99 = \\$249.99** missing in QBO\n\n---\n\n### 4) How this ties to the overall difference\n\n- Partial shortfalls: **\\$62.50**\n- Unmatched shortfalls: **\\$249.99**  \n- Total variance: **\\$62.50 + \\$249.99 = \\$312.49**, which exactly matches the tool’s total difference between invoiced and QBO.\n\n---\n\n### 5) File/tool output\n\nI’ve already saved the full reconciliation (all 84 lines) via the tool. Each row includes:\n- `vendor`\n- `period`\n- `invoice_amount`\n- `qbo_amount`\n- `status` (Matched / Partial / Unmatched)\n- `notes` (e.g., “\\$12.50 short in QBO”, “No matching QBO entry”)\n\nPath from the tool:\n- `.../output/reconciliation_output.csv`\n\nIf you’d like, I can next generate a formatted Excel reconciliation report and/or summarize the discrepancies by vendor or quarter.', 'type': 'output_text', 'logprobs': []}], 'role': 'assistant', 'status': 'completed', 'type': 'message'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'How confident are you in your reconciliation results? Rate your confidence (0-100%) and identify any areas of uncertainty.'}], 'instructions': 'You are a financial reconciliation analyst. The input files include a QBO expense report and vendor invoices. You also have a tool to save reconciliation results. Your job is to read invoices and the QBO expense report, then match vendors across the two sources and compare amounts.\n\nSteps:\n1. Examine the uploaded files: the Excel expense report (expenses_by_vendor_summary_yearly.xlsx)    and the invoice PDFs.\n2. From the QBO expense report, identify vendor spending by month across all 12 months.\n3. From each invoice PDF, extract vendor name, period, and total amount.\n4. Match invoice vendors to QBO vendors — names may differ between sources.    Use your judgment to map them.\n5. For each matched pair, note the invoice amount and the corresponding QBO amount.\n6. Save the reconciliation results — the tool will compute exact/partial/unmatched status.\n\nReal-world QBO exports are messy. Vendor names may be abbreviated or inconsistent, expenses may be split across line items, payments can post in the wrong month, and refunds or credits may appear as separate rows. Account for these when matching.\n\nYou are responsible for vendor name matching and period mapping. The save tool handles the numerical comparison and status classification.\n\nWhen saving results, use the invoice vendor name and format period as "Mon YYYY" (e.g. "Jan 2025", "Feb 2025", "Dec 2025").\n', 'model': 'gpt-5.1', 'tools': [{'name': 'save_reconciliation', 'parameters': {'properties': {'reconciliation_json': {'title': 'Reconciliation Json', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['reconciliation_json'], 'title': 'save_reconciliation_args', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'strict': True, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Save reconciliation results. You provide matched pairs (vendor, period, invoice_amount, qbo_amount); the tool computes match status and saves CSV.'}, {'name': 'create_reconciliation_excel', 'parameters': {'properties': {'reconciliation_csv_path': {'default': 'output/reconciliation_output.csv', 'title': 'Reconciliation Csv Path', 'type': 'string'}, 'output_filename': {'default': 'reconciliation_report.xlsx', 'title': 'Output Filename', 'type': 'string'}}, 'title': 'create_reconciliation_excel_args', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['reconciliation_csv_path', 'output_filename']}, 'strict': True, 'type': 'function', 'description': 'Create a styled Excel reconciliation report with color-coded match status.'}]}}
